Changes
-------

The material from python-ftfy was translated from Python to R and modified.
It is not the original. The translation and the modifications are

    Copyright 2026 Edward Barker

under the same licence. The port was written with AI assistance.

Every place where the package knowingly behaves differently from
python-ftfy v6.3.1 is recorded in the departure registry: one file for each
departure in the directory `departures` of the installed package
(`inst/departures/` in the source repository).

Each derived source file starts with a line naming the python-ftfy file it
came from.


Derived from python-ftfy
------------------------

Source: python-ftfy v6.3.1, https://github.com/rspeer/python-ftfy
Copyright 2023 Robyn Speer
Licence: Apache-2.0

1. Copied unchanged

   tests/testthat/upstream/test_cases.json
       python-ftfy's tests/test_cases.json, byte for byte. The README beside
       it says where it came from.

2. Translated to R and modified

   R/*.R
       Translated from the Python modules in python-ftfy's ftfy/
       directory. The first line of each file names its source. The few
       files with nothing from python-ftfy have no such line.

   man/*.Rd
       Documentation, in part adapted from python-ftfy's docstrings and
       built from the comments in R/*.R.

   tests/testthat/*.R
       Tests, in part translated from python-ftfy's tests/ and from the
       doctests in ftfy/. A translated test file starts with the line naming
       its source, and each translated test names the upstream file and
       line.

3. Read or generated from python-ftfy by running it

   R/sysdata.rda
       Internal data read from python-ftfy: the text of its regular
       expressions, rewritten for the ICU regex engine, and its data
       tables, among them one decoding table for each single-byte codec it
       uses. This file carries no notice of its own.

   tests/testthat/reference/*
       Snapshots of what python-ftfy v6.3.1 returns for the test inputs.

   The scripts that write these files are in the directory `data-raw/` of
   the source repository, https://github.com/epabarker/r-ftfy, and are not
   part of the built package. Each starts with the line naming its source,
   and `data-raw/README.md` gives the exact commands that run them.


Other sources
-------------

The following are named as sources of the data in group 3. They are facts
about mappings, observed by running python-ftfy v6.3.1 on CPython 3.13
(Unicode 15.1.0). No source code or data file of CPython or of the Unicode
Consortium is copied into the package, so they are sources and not
licensors, and no licence of theirs applies to the package.

   CPython
       The codec tables give the code point that each byte decodes to
       under CPython's charmap codecs, which python-ftfy uses and extends.
       CPython builds those codecs from mapping files published by the
       Unicode Consortium and by Microsoft. Where the package reproduces
       how Python resolves an HTML numeric character reference, that was
       observed from `html.unescape`.

   Unicode data
       The sets of characters that Python's regex classes \s, \w and \d
       match are written into the regular expressions as code-point sets,
       as observed on CPython 3.13 with Unicode 15.1.0.


